+### Voyage: Root index.html spec
+
+**Problem:** Opening the app in a real web browser shows a blank page. No `index.html` exists at the project root. The test harness reads `js/index.html` directly, so all 30 existing DOM scenarios pass, but the product has no browser entry point.
+
+**Action:** Authored `features/root-index-html.feature` with one scenario that asserts the root `index.html` exists, contains a script tag loading `js/app.js`, and carries the core TodoMVC sections (`.todoapp`, `.new-todo`, `.todo-list`). Added filesystem-based step definitions to `features/support/steps.js`. Updated `watchbill.json` with a new `root-entry-point` watch at position 1.
+
+**Verification:** Scenario fails red as expected -- `Given the root index.html exists at the project root` asserts file existence and the file is absent. Dry-run: 31 scenarios, 125 steps, all parsable.
+
+**Handoff to QM:** Red target is `features/root-index-html.feature:Root index.html exists with correct structure and script`. Crew must create a root `index.html` built from `assets/app-template.index.html` that loads `js/app.js` via a script tag. The scenario will go green when the file exists with the correct structure.
